I think I’ve found the root cause. The issue lies in [this line](https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/structured-merge-diff/blob/ccf7a061f165cd3feee92af191157c053154d8bc/merge/update.go#L104).When the object needs conversion and the request is targeting the status subresource, changes to spec should be discarded. However, the converted version is used here, which causes s.IgnoreFilter[managerSet.APIVersion()] to be nil. As a result, the apply ManagedFields entry is dropped.

I think this should be changed to:
```
// Due to the fact that IgnoreFilter originates from resetFields,
// the API endpoint only includes the resetFields of the current version,
// which results in the inability to filter the data corresponding to the version conversion,
// leading to incorrect manager field updates.
versions[managerSet.APIVersion()] = compare.FilterFields(s.IgnoreFilter[version])
```
This way, the IgnoreFilter is still retrieved based on the API endpoint’s requested version.
I’d greatly appreciate any suggestions you may have.
